# Security Rules

## Authentication

- Every route that accesses user data must call `getUserFromSession(request)` and return 401 if null.
- Import from `@/lib/server/auth`, never redefine the session parser.
- The `session` cookie is HMAC-signed (`SESSION_SECRET`, or derived from `API_KEY_SECRET`). Set it only with `setSessionCookie` and clear it with `clearSessionCookie`; never write it by hand.
- Hash passwords with `hashPassword` / `verifyPassword` from `@/lib/server/password` (salted scrypt).

## Authorization / Ownership

- Before returning, updating, or deleting a chat/story, verify `String(doc.user_id) === sessionUser.id`.
- Return 403 (Forbidden) if ownership check fails — never silently skip.

## API Keys

- User API keys are encrypted with AES-256 before storage (`lib/server/crypto.ts`).
- Full API keys are only returned during hydration (`?hydrate=1`), not on every profile GET.
- The `API_KEY_SECRET` env var must be set in both `.env.local` and Vercel project settings.

## Redirects

- Never hardcode `http://localhost:3000` in redirects. Use `new URL('/', request.url)`.

## Prompts

- System prompts live in `lib/server/prompts/` and are never sent to the client. Client sends `promptParams` only.
